Yes — this is **composite types** (MongoDB-only), defined with `type` instead of `model`:

```prisma
model User {
  id      String  @id @default(auto()) @map("_id") @db.ObjectId
  name    String
  address Address
}

type Address {
  country String
  // ...other fields
}
```

`Address` here is embedded directly in the `User` document (no separate collection, no `@relation`).

Source: `prisma/apps/docs/content/docs/orm/v7/prisma-client/special-fields-and-types/composite-types.mdx`, "Composite types" intro + example schema (lines 9–80). Note: this only works with the MongoDB provider, not relational databases like PostgreSQL.

